{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1030005-2e-how-to-master-the-role","id":1030005,"title":"[2E] How to master the Role?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-11T04:56:22-08:00","id":1030005,"title":"[2E] How to master the Role?","content":"So how does mastering the Role works in the 2E <b>Promethean</b>? From what I read, each Role has 2 special Milestones and 1 unique Breaking Point. If my character fulfills one of Milestones, she has 'mastered the Role', am I right? How character is feeling then? She get's special Elpis Vision, or just feel that Vitriol is generating in his body?<br /> <br /> For example, I have Golem on Plumbum starting his Pilgrimage as player. He did not choose Role he is study, yet, but is possible that he will fulfill Milestone for one of them by events in game. He is kidnapped by Alchemist that has Athanor in her 'collection'. If he will be free by his buddy mages, will he master Chronicler Role just by finding Athanor? Even by looking on it, not even <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronicler Role</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Milestones:</b> Discover a hidden or lost Athanor. Discover enough of other Created\u2019s Pilgrimages to discover underlying commonalities.<br /> <b>Breaking point: </b>Discard the information you have gathered as inapplicable to your Pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about other Roles in Plumbum - They all are about other Created. As PC is only Promethean in chronicle world ( in nearby, at least ) can those Milestones be changed to accommodate shearing knowledge with mages or humans?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T13:30:39-08:00","id":1031305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1030005-2e-how-to-master-the-role#post1030005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how does mastering the Role works in the 2E <b>Promethean</b>? From what I read, each Role has 2 special Milestones and 1 unique Breaking Point. If my character fulfills one of Milestones, she has 'mastered the Role', am I right? How character is feeling then? She get's special Elpis Vision, or just feel that Vitriol is generating in his body?<br /> <br /> For example, I have Golem on Plumbum starting his Pilgrimage as player. He did not choose Role he is study, yet, but is possible that he will fulfill Milestone for one of them by events in game. He is kidnapped by Alchemist that has Athanor in her 'collection'. If he will be free by his buddy mages, will he master Chronicler Role just by finding Athanor? Even by looking on it, not even<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What about other Roles in Plumbum - They all are about other Created. As PC is only Promethean in chronicle world ( in nearby, at least ) can those Milestones be changed to accommodate shearing knowledge with mages or humans?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not quite.<br /> <br /> Read the sections on p. 179 under the &quot;Turning Away&quot; and &quot;Taking a Role&quot; headers. You can't fulfill a Role's milestone if you're not pursuing it; some of them are even mutually exclusive. <br /> <br /> Also, note that the milestones under the Roles are suggestions. Your ST should be tailoring a milestone to represent mastery of a particular Role, and it's going to be different for different characters. As an example, two of the PCs in my game have mastered Sage. One is a Frankenstein who mastered all three of the Roles in Cuprum; he's a bounty hunter and a gunslinger. The other is an Osiran who wants to learn the creation procedure for all the known Lineages. I had to approach their milestones pretty differently. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}